/-! # Derived descent for a representable hypercover of a site

Source: Stacks Project, `spaces-simplicial.tex`, Tag 0D8N, lemma-hypercovering-X-simple-
descent-bounded-abelian (bounded-below case), section-hypercovering
(blueprint: lem-trf-site-hypercover-derived-descent).

The source category is the category of abelian sheaves on the total simplicial
site constructed in `SimplicialSliceSite`. Restriction along its projection is
the augmentation inverse image. The adjunction is therefore fixed by `U`.

The proof follows Tag 0D8G. (1) Slice localization identifies each base-changed
matching object and its covering sieve. (2) Exact restriction to a slice preserves
injectives, and the localization Cech complex computes the direct image of an
injective. (3) Hypercover section exactness makes that complex exact objectwise.
(4) Grothendieck sheaf categories provide bounded-below injective representatives.
(5) Leray's acyclic-complex comparison identifies the resulting chain map with the
ordinary derived adjunction unit and proves it is an isomorphism.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- Enough injectives on the small total slice site, with its explicit small-site
universe. Source: Stacks, Tag 079H; the Grothendieck category construction and
site enough-injectives theorem in step 4
(blueprint: lem-trf-site-hypercover-derived-descent). -/
instance SimplicialSliceSite.total_enoughInjectives
    {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    {X : C} (U : SimplicialObject (Over X)) :
    EnoughInjectives (Sheaf (SimplicialSliceSite.topology J
      (SimplicialSliceSite.underlying U)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :=
  IsGrothendieckAbelian.enoughInjectives.{u}


/-- Derived cohomological descent along a representable hypercover of a site.

The simplicial object is given in the slice `Over X`, so its augmentation is the
structure map to `X`; this is equivalent to a simplicial object of `C` equipped
with a natural map to the constant object `X`. The cones `M n` are the finite
matching limits over all proper faces in `Over X`, and `hcover` says that the sieve
generated by each matching arrow is covering for the induced slice topology.
The comma total site gives families of sheaves on the slices, with transition
maps induced by its arrows and coherence induced by composition. The augmentation
inverse image is restriction along the explicit projection to `Over X`; its
ordinary adjunction on abelian sheaves is `SimplicialSliceSite.abelianAdjunction`.
The bounded-below derived adjunction uses this exact inverse image.

Proof: (1) For `T → X`, identify the slice of `C/X` with `C/T`. Matching
objects base change to `T ×_X M_n`, including degree zero, so the pulled-back
matching sieves cover. (2) Site restriction preserves injectives by its exact
left adjoint. The site sheaf categories have enough injectives, and localization
of an injective is acyclic. The acyclic Cech computation of the augmentation
therefore has sections `I(T ×_X U_p)` for an injective `I`.
(3) Injective hypercover section exactness makes this augmented complex exact on
every `T`. The triangle identity identifies its degree-zero augmentation with
the ordinary unit. That unit is an isomorphism on injectives and their pulled-back
sheaves have no higher direct images. (4) The abelian sheaf categories are
Grothendieck; choose a bounded-below injective representative `I` of `E`. Exact
inverse image preserves this representative and its terms are direct-image
acyclic by (3). (5) Leray's acyclic-complex comparison identifies the termwise
unit followed by the derived comparison with the ordinary derived adjunction
unit (computed by an injective replacement). The former is a quasi-isomorphism
by (3), hence the specified unit is an isomorphism.
Source: Stacks Project, `spaces-simplicial.tex`, Tag 0D8N and Tag 0D8G
(blueprint: lem-trf-site-hypercover-derived-descent). -/
theorem derivedDescent_of_site_hypercover
    {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] [HasFiniteLimits C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (X : C)
    (U : SimplicialObject (Over X))
    (M : ∀ n : ℕ, Cone (SimplicialObject.properFaceDiagram U n))
    (hM : ∀ n : ℕ, IsLimit (M n))
    (μ : ∀ n : ℕ, U.obj (op (SimplexCategory.mk n)) ⟶ (M n).pt)
    (hμ : ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : SimplicialObject.ProperFaceCategory n),
      μ n ≫ (M n).π.app (op a) = U.map a.obj.hom.op)
    (hcover : ∀ n : ℕ,
      Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton (μ n)) ∈ (J.over X) ((M n).pt))
    (E : DerivedCategory.Plus (Sheaf (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u})) :
    IsIso ((SimplicialSliceSite.abelianAdjunction J U).derivedPlus.unit.app E) := by
  sorry

end CategoryTheory
